 "method": "Jammer: noise-like, isotropic, at 20 N 132 E (Philippine Sea), 10 kHz at 301.005 MHz or 25 kHz at 301.000 MHz (shared-1, relayed by all three satellites); reference carriers removed. Nominal: the EIRP at which the mean per-bin excess of the jammer over the floor (site noise plus relayed transponder noise) reaches 10 log10(10^(threshold_db/10) - 1) dB, i.e. half of its bins cross the tracker's threshold (threshold_db 6 dB at navg 8: 4.75 dB per bin, C/N0 44.8 dB-Hz in 10 kHz, 48.7 dB-Hz in 25 kHz), from linkbudget.path_budget. Tracker: the server's SignalTracker (server.pipeline.detection) fed 20 simulated PSD frames (SimWorld.render_psd, 10 s at 2 Hz) of the channel's derived monitor from four start times 10 minutes apart, bisected to 0.25 dB: 'full width' is the weakest EIRP at which one confirmed detection covers at least 80 % of the jammer's band in at least 3 of the 4 looks (a usable detection: the event gets the right uplink range); 'fragments' the weakest at which any confirmed detection overlaps the band in 3 of 4 (near it the tracker reports scattered detections a few bins wide). Every channel is given the antenna under test (dishes: no polarisation loss; beam: 3 dB, linear on circular), pointed at its satellite as configured.",
